    },
    {
      "text": "visual observations into compact latent tokens zt = E(ot | o<t) ∈RN×C, where N is the number of spatial tokens",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "at ∈RD via a lightweight MLP ϕ(·) where D is the dimension of the video token after patchfication, enabling unified",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "coordinates), so the action history a<t effectively captures the trajectory of the embodiment’s configuration. Conditioning",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "zt+1:t+K ∼pθ(· | z≤t, a<t),",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "The action history a<t encodes the embodiment’s state trajectory for determining feasible actions, while the observation",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "history z<t provides temporal context for multi-step interactions (e.g., whether an object was previously grasped). We",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "at:t+K−1 ∼gψ(· | ˆzt+1:t+K, z≤t, a<t),",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "observation history z≤t, and action history a<t. This mirrors recent IDM-based policies [1, 20, 22, 55, 73] that leverage",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "scenes evolve gradually. We sparsify the video sequence by temporally downsampling frames by a factor of τ = 4,",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "according to the action dimension, then apply a scaling factor α =",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "range during training. By training with variable chunk sizes (e.g., K ∈[1, 8]), the model learns to generate coherent",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "use K = 4 for deployment as a practical trade-off.",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "randomly augment the video history z≤t with noise following the same interpolation scheme as flow matching:",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "˜z≤t =",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "(1 −saug)ϵ + saugz≤t,",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "p = 0.5,",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "saug ∈[0.5, 1], ϵ ∼N(0, I)",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "z≤t,",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "1 −p = 0.5",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "At inference time, this enables a significant speedup: instead of fully denoising video tokens from s = 0 to s = 1,",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "we only need to denoise to s = 0.5, halving the number of denoising steps for video generation while maintaining action",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "▷Generate video chunk (integrate to s = 0.5)",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "▷Generate action chunk (integrate to s = 1)",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "for i = t to t + K −1 do",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "Ldyn = Et,s,zt+1,ϵ",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "t+1, s, ˜z≤t, a<t|c) −˙z(s)",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "where s ∈[0, 1] is flow time, z(s)",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "t+1 = (1 −s)ϵ + szt+1 with ϵ ∼N(0, I), ˙z(s)",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "t+1 = zt+1 −ϵ, ˜z≤t is the augmented history",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "Linv = Et,s,at,ϵ",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "t , s, ˜z≤t+1, a<t|c) −˙a(s)",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "= (1 −s)ϵ + sat with ϵ ∼N(0, I), ˜zt, ˜zt+1 are the (potentially noisy) current and next video tokens, and c",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "is the language instruction. The complete objective is L = Ldyn + λLinv.",
      "section_id": "sec:method",
      "page_start": 4,
      "page_end": 9
    },
    {
      "text": "if t > 0 then",
      "section_id": "sec:model",
      "page_start": 9,
      "page_end": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "Lfdm = Et,s,ˆzt+1,ϵ",
      "section_id": "sec:model",
      "page_start": 9,
      "page_end": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "∥vψ(˜zt+1, s, zt, at, ˜z<t, ˆa<t|c) −˙z(s)",
      "section_id": "sec:model",
      "page_start": 9,
      "page_end": 10
    },
    {
      "text": "systems is: 7EEF + 7joints + 1gripper per arm, resulting in (7 + 7 + 1) × 2 = 30 dimensions.",
      "section_id": "sec:experiments",
      "page_start": 10,
      "page_end": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "We use Wan2.2-5B as the backbone for the video stream, with hidden dimension dv = 3072",
      "section_id": "sec:experiments",
      "page_start": 10,
      "page_end": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "and 30 transformer layers. The action stream shares the same depth but uses a reduced hidden dimension da = 768",
      "section_id": "sec:experiments",
      "page_start": 10,
      "page_end": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "dimension, resulting in a total of N = 192 spatial tokens per frame. The action encoder ϕ and decoder are implemented",
      "section_id": "sec:experiments",
      "page_start": 10,
      "page_end": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "For inference, we use Euler solver with 3 steps for video tokens (integrating to s = 0.6) and 10 steps for action",
      "section_id": "sec:experiments",
      "page_start": 10,
      "page_end": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "tokens (integrating to s = 1.0). Video CFG scale is set to 5.0, while action CFG scale is set to 1.0. During training,",
      "section_id": "sec:experiments",
      "page_start": 10,
      "page_end": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "noise augmentation is applied with probability p = 0.5 and saug ∼Uniform[0.5, 1.0]. Following LLM practices, we",
      "section_id": "sec:experiments",
      "page_start": 10,
      "page_end": 12
    },
    {
      "text": "seed comprising 500 evaluation trials (totally 3 × 500 = 1500) for every task suite.",
      "section_id": "sec:results",
      "page_start": 13,
      "page_end": 13
    },
    {
      "text": "Average Horizon = 1",
      "section_id": "sec:results-2",
      "page_start": 13,
      "page_end": 14
    },
    {
      "text": "Average Horizon = 2",
      "section_id": "sec:results-2",
      "page_start": 13,
      "page_end": 14
    },
    {
      "text": "Average Horizon = 3",
      "section_id": "sec:results-2",
      "page_start": 13,
      "page_end": 14
    },
    {
      "text": "π0.5, X-VLA, and Motus. Notably, the improvement becomes more pronounced for longer-horizon tasks: at Horizon =",
      "section_id": "sec:methods",
      "page_start": 14,
      "page_end": 14
    },
    {
      "text": "Easy Horizon = 1",
      "section_id": "sec:ablation-2",
      "page_start": 15,
      "page_end": 15
    },
    {
      "text": "Easy Horizon = 2",
      "section_id": "sec:ablation-2",
      "page_start": 15,
      "page_end": 15
    },
    {
      "text": "Easy Horizon = 3",
      "section_id": "sec:ablation-2",
      "page_start": 15,
      "page_end": 15
    },
    {
      "text": "scaling factor α =",
      "section_id": "sec:ablation-2",
      "page_start": 15,
      "page_end": 15
    },
    {
      "text": "percentage: PS = Average Progress",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix",
      "page_start": 23,
      "page_end": 31
    },
    {
      "text": "SR = # Successful Trials",
      "section_id": "sec:appendix",
